+# Subagent model labels
+
+`task.hideModelProviderPrefixes` removes selected leading provider IDs from Subagent model labels.
+The source default is `[]`, so unconfigured installations keep complete labels.
+
+```yaml
+task:
+  showResolvedModelBadge: true
+  hideModelProviderPrefixes:
+    - anthropic
+    - openai-codex
+```
+
+- Values are exact, case-sensitive provider IDs without `/`, whitespace, or control characters.
+- Only the leading provider segment is removed; other providers and all model suffixes stay visible.
+- The policy applies to the Subagent HUD, Task and Wait badges, and native Task model labels.
+- Existing visibility controls and normal settings-layer precedence remain in effect.
+- Live configuration changes refresh mutable views without resetting previously accepted terminal history.
+- Accepted rows keep their painted labels, including during later replay and width reflow.
+- Model selection, routing, recorded identities, session data, and the Main status line remain unchanged.
+
+With this configuration, `openai-codex/gpt-6-luna` becomes `gpt-6-luna` in model labels.
+`anthropic/claude-opus-5-5` becomes `claude-opus-5-5`, while `openai/gpt-5.2` remains unchanged.
+Set the list to `[]` to restore full labels in mutable views.
+
+The configuration is read through the existing Settings loader and live file watcher.
+Install a version that registers this setting before activating it in managed configuration.
